§§ `Section 334(b) and section 1 — "employee"`

GIVEN e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      k IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person who works`
`a worker, employed:` e `family:` f `regularly:` r `in an employee's work:` w `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` k MEANS
    `A person who works` WITH
        `employed within an employment relationship`                                    IS e
        `a parent, child, grandchild, brother or sister of the relative employing them` IS f
        `works in the enterprise regularly`                                             IS r
        `in work which, had they not done it, would have been done by an employee`      IS w
        `wage fixed in a Law or in or under a resolution of the Knesset`                IS k

#ASSERT     `s 1 — the person is an employee` (`a worker, employed:` TRUE `family:` FALSE `regularly:` FALSE `in an employee's work:` FALSE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 1 — the person is an employee` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` TRUE `regularly:` TRUE `in an employee's work:` TRUE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the person is an employee` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` TRUE `regularly:` FALSE `in an employee's work:` TRUE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the person is an employee` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` TRUE `regularly:` TRUE `in an employee's work:` FALSE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the person is an employee` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` FALSE `regularly:` TRUE `in an employee's work:` TRUE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` FALSE)
-- A person whose wage is fixed by a Knesset resolution: not an employee under s 1 alone, an
-- employee for Chapter 15 by s 334(b).
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the person is an employee` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` FALSE `regularly:` FALSE `in an employee's work:` FALSE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` TRUE)
#ASSERT     `s 334(b) — the person is an employee for Chapter 15` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` FALSE `regularly:` FALSE `in an employee's work:` FALSE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 334(b) — the person is an employee for Chapter 15` (`a worker, employed:` FALSE `family:` FALSE `regularly:` FALSE `in an employee's work:` FALSE `wage fixed by Law or Knesset:` FALSE)

§§ `Section 1 — "self-employed person"`

GIVEN n IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's occupation in a period`
`an occupation, not as an employee:` n `hours a week:` h `monthly income:` i MEANS
    `A person's occupation in a period` WITH
        `engaged in the period in an occupation not as an employee` IS n
        `average hours a week in the occupation`                    IS h
        `average monthly income from the occupation`                IS i

-- With the average wage at 13,566 (the Institute's 2026 figure under s 1) and the Schedule A sum
-- at 15% of it, 2,034.9 (Schedule A, source line 4365, read for a quarter beginning in 2026).
`the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566` MEANS 15% TIMES 13566

-- (1) at least twenty hours: 20 is enough, 19.9 is not (with low income).
#ASSERT     `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 20 `monthly income:` 1000) `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 19.9 `monthly income:` 1000) `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`
-- (2) income not less than 50% of the average wage: 6,783 is enough, 6,782.99 is not (10 hours).
#ASSERT     `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 10 `monthly income:` 6783)    `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 10 `monthly income:` 6782.99) `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "self-employed person" (2) — average monthly income of` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 10 `monthly income:` 6782.99) `not less than 50% of the average wage of` 13566
-- (3) twelve hours and the Schedule A sum: 12 hours and 2,034.9 is enough; 11.99 hours is not.
#ASSERT     `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 12 `monthly income:` 2034.9) `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` TRUE `hours a week:` 11.99 `monthly income:` 2034.9) `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`
-- The occupation must be followed not as an employee.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — a self-employed person in the period:` (`an occupation, not as an employee:` FALSE `hours a week:` 40 `monthly income:` 20000) `with the average wage at` 13566 `and the Schedule A sum at` `the Schedule A sum at 15% of 13,566`

§§ `Section 1 — "the average wage", "update day", "the Minister"`

-- SCENARIO data: three months at 13,000, 13,300 and 13,600 average 13,300; compensation of 2%
-- adds 266.
`three months of CBS figures and 2% compensation` MEANS
    `The data for an update of the average wage` WITH
        `CBS average wage per employee post, first of the three months`                IS 13000
        `CBS average wage per employee post, second of the three months`               IS 13300
        `CBS average wage per employee post, third of the three months`                IS 13600
        `compensation rate given from the end of those three months to the update day` IS 2%

#ASSERT `s 1 "the average wage" (1) — the wage average, from` `three months of CBS figures and 2% compensation` EQUALS 13300
#ASSERT `s 1 — the average wage on an update day, from` `three months of CBS figures and 2% compensation` EQUALS 13566
#ASSERT `s 1 — the update days of the average wage in tax year` 2026 `with compensation applying in months` (LIST 7) EQUALS LIST (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the update days of the average wage in tax year` 2027 `with compensation applying in months` EMPTY EQUALS LIST (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — "the Minister"` EQUALS "the Minister of Labour and Welfare"

